# TEMPLATE ONLY — Vite never reads this file.
#
# Vite only loads: .env, .env.local, .env.production, .env.development
# (and their .local variants). Putting real values in THIS file has no
# effect on any build. For local development, copy it first:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Find both values in your Supabase project: Settings -> API.
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL             e.g. https://xxxxx.supabase.co
#   VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY the "anon" / "publishable" public key
#
# These are read at BUILD time. Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the
# JavaScript bundle when you run `npm run build`, so changing them requires
# a rebuild/redeploy to take effect.
#
# NEVER put the service_role / secret key in this file or in any variable
# prefixed with VITE_ — anything with that prefix is bundled into the
# client-side JavaScript and shipped to every visitor's browser.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
